# Glossary for new words

When a change adds a feature, screen, or user-facing copy that introduces a word users have to learn, check `evo-lift/app/glossary/page.tsx` before finishing.

## Add a term when

- The word is a product term the UI uses — a name, label, or abbreviation — and the glossary does not already define it.
- Examples that belong: Session, Template, Lift, Loaded (kg), 1RM, ExRx, Compound.

## Skip the glossary when

- The word is an ordinary control or sentence, such as Save, Cancel, Clear filters, or an error message.
- It is an internal code name that never appears in the UI.
- The glossary already defines it. Reuse that wording. Do not add a second name for the same thing.

## How to write the entry

- Follow `evo-lift/BRAND_GUIDELINES.md`. Use the same words the UI uses.
- One short definition in plain language. Static copy only. Do not load sessions, templates, or goals.
- Insert the entry in alphabetical order by the term.
- If the UI already links the term out, as with ExRx.net, keep that link in the definition.
